.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
backend.hcl
*.tfvars.json

# terraform.tfvars is committed HERE on purpose, overriding `**/terraform.tfvars` in
# infra/.gitignore (and `infra/**/terraform.tfvars` in the root one — which is why the negation has
# to live in this file, deeper than both). Every value in it is a public repo Actions variable, and
# its absence is the whole defect: the three deployer-role ARNs are `count`-gated on it, so a bare
# apply from a fresh checkout planned their DESTRUCTION. See README.md.
!terraform.tfvars
